To display the most commonly used verb tense and its frequency percentage in a given sentence using NLP POS tagging, you can use the `PosTagger` PHP library that you mentioned. Here's an example code that demonstrates how to achieve this:
```php
<?php
require_once('path/to/PosTagger.php');
// example sentence
$sentence = "I have been studying for my exams and will continue to do so until they are over.";
// initialize the PosTagger object
$tagger = new PosTagger();
// get the POS tags for the sentence
$tags = $tagger->tag($sentence);
// initialize an array to store the verb tenses and their frequency
$verb_tenses = array();
// loop through the tags and extract the verb tenses
foreach ($tags as $tag) {
  if ($tag['pos'] == 'VB' || $tag['pos'] == 'VBD' || $tag['pos'] == 'VBG' || $tag['pos'] == 'VBN' || $tag['pos'] == 'VBP' || $tag['pos'] == 'VBZ') {
    $verb_tense = $tag['tense'];
    if (isset($verb_tenses[$verb_tense])) {
      $verb_tenses[$verb_tense]++;
    } else {
      $verb_tenses[$verb_tense] = 1;
    }
  }
}
// calculate the total number of verbs in the sentence
$total_verbs = array_sum($verb_tenses);
// calculate the percentage of each verb tense
foreach ($verb_tenses as $tense => $count) {
  $percentage = round(($count / $total_verbs) * 100, 2);
  echo "$tense: $percentage%\n";
}
?>
```
In this example, we first initialize the `PosTagger` object and use it to get the POS tags for the given sentence. We then loop through the tags and extract the verb tenses, storing them in an array along with their frequency. Finally, we calculate the percentage of each verb tense and display the results.
As for implementing the `PosTagger` library in your code, you can download the library from the GitHub repository you mentioned and include the `PosTagger.php` file in your PHP code using the `require_once` statement, as shown in the example code above. Just make sure to update the path to the `PosTagger.php` file to match the location on your server.

