```
#include <iostream>
#include <thread>
#include <vector>
void process_review(int review_id) {
    // process review with given id
}
int main() {
    int num_reviews = 1000; // replace with actual number of reviews
    int num_threads = 4; // replace with desired number of threads
    std::vector<std::thread> threads;
    for (int i = 0; i < num_reviews; i++) {
        threads.push_back(std::thread(process_review, i));
        if (threads.size() == num_threads) {
            for (auto& thread : threads) {
                thread.join();
            }
            threads.clear();
        }
    }
    for (auto& thread : threads) {
        thread.join();
    }
    return 0;
}
```
This code creates a vector of threads and processes each review in a separate thread. The `num_threads` variable determines how many threads to use at a time. Once the vector of threads reaches the desired size, the program waits for all threads to finish before clearing the vector and starting the next batch of threads.
