To identify the domain name of a website URL and gather information about its hosting provider, SSL certificate status, and any potential subdomains or redirects associated with it using Swift, you can use a networking library such as Alamofire or URLSession to make HTTP requests to the website and parse the response data.
Here's a sample code that uses Alamofire to retrieve information about a website:
```swift
import Alamofire
import SwiftyJSON
let url = "https://www.example.com"
// Make an HTTP GET request to the website
Alamofire.request(url).responseString { response in
    guard let html = response.result.value else {
        print("Error retrieving website HTML")
        return
    }

    // Parse the HTML to extract the domain name
    let domain = url.components(separatedBy: "://")[1].components(separatedBy: "/")[0]

    // Use regular expressions to extract information about the website
    let regex = try! NSRegularExpression(pattern: "<title>(.*?)</title>")
    let title = regex.firstMatch(in: html, range: NSRange(html.startIndex..., in: html))
        .map { String(html[Range($0.range, in: html)!]) }
        .map { $0.replacingOccurrences(of: "<[^>]+>", with: "", options: .regularExpression, range: nil) }

    // Print the results
    print("Domain: \(domain)")
    print("Title: \(title ?? "N/A")")
}
```
This code retrieves the HTML of the website at the specified URL using Alamofire, extracts the domain name from the URL, and uses regular expressions to extract the website's title from the HTML. You can modify this code to extract other information such as SSL certificate status, subdomains, and redirects.

