How can I calculate the exact duration, in days, between January 1st and April 5th, inclusive, while taking into account any potential leap years and daylight saving time adjustments that may have occurred during this time period? Additionally, how can I ensure that the calculated duration accounts for the effect of time zone changes that occurred during this period, as well as any historical changes to time zones that may have affected the region in question? Finally, can you provide me with the output in a table that clearly indicates the number of days for each month, as well as any adjustments made for leap years, daylight saving time, and time zone changes, along with the PHP code used to make these calculations and any relevant explanations of the methodology employed?
Here is the PHP code that can accomplish this task:
$start_date = new DateTime('January 1st');
$end_date = new DateTime('April 5th');
$interval = DateInterval::createFromDateString('1 day');
$period = new DatePeriod($start_date, $interval, $end_date);
$table_data = array();
foreach($period as $date) {
  $month = $date->format('F');
  $day = $date->format('d');
  $year = $date->format('Y');
  $timezone = new DateTimeZone('America/New_York');
  $datetime = new DateTime("$month $day, $year", $timezone);
  $dst = $datetime->format('I');
  $days_in_month = cal_days_in_month(CAL_GREGORIAN, $datetime->format('m'), $datetime->format('Y'));
  if($dst) {
    $hours_to_add = 1;
  } else {
    $hours_to_add = 0;
  }
  $timezone_offset = $timezone->getOffset($datetime) / 3600;
  $table_data[$month]['days']++;
  $table_data[$month]['leap_year_adjustment'] += intval(date('L', strtotime("$month $day, $year")));
  $table_data[$month]['dst_adjustment'] += $hours_to_add;
  $table_data[$month]['timezone_adjustment'] += $timezone_offset;
  $table_data[$month]['total_days'] += $days_in_month;
}
echo '<table>';
echo '<tr><th>Month</th><th>Days in Month</th><th>Leap Year Adjustment</th><th>DST Adjustment</th><th>Timezone Adjustment</th><th>Total Days</th></tr>';
foreach($table_data as $month_name => $data) {
  echo '<tr>';
  echo "<td>$month_name</td>";
  echo "<td>{$data['days']}</td>";
  echo "<td>{$data['leap_year_adjustment']}</td>";
  echo "<td>{$data['dst_adjustment']}</td>";
  echo "<td>{$data['timezone_adjustment']}</td>";
  echo "<td>{$data['total_days']}</td>";
  echo '</tr>';
}
echo '</table>';
